# Build context of the backend image:
#   docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .
# (.github/workflows/backend.yml; the context is the repository root because
# the backend depends on rust/wasm-programs/pkg by path).
#
# This is an allow-list: everything is excluded, then the few paths the image
# needs are let back in. That keeps .git, build/, rust/target/, versions/,
# wasm-bin/, runs/, src/, docs/, the jars, the Gradle and node caches and
# every other directory out of the context without naming each one, and stays
# correct when new top-level directories appear.
#
# What cargo needs to resolve `pkg` from outside the rust/ workspace (tested
# with a copy holding only these paths, see docs/DEPLOY.md, "Build context"):
#   - rust/Cargo.toml: pkg inherits `workspace = true` dependencies, so cargo
#     must read the workspace root manifest. It does NOT load the other ~150
#     members for this, so their directories are not needed.
#   - rust/wasm-programs/pkg and the crates it depends on by path
#     (ecm-host-abi, ecm-ssh-crypto, ecm-disco), all under rust/crates/.
# If the backend ever becomes a member of the rust/ workspace, or cargo is run
# from inside rust/, every member's Cargo.toml is required and this file must
# change.

*

!backend
!rust/Cargo.toml
!rust/Cargo.lock
!rust/crates
!rust/wasm-programs/pkg

# Never part of the image, wherever they are.
**/target
**/.git
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.jar
**/node_modules
